entre of the leaf rosette and are carried on 15 - 20cm tall erect stems. Apple green pouch (or slipper) is a modification of lip that traps insects and consequently provides an ''escape route'' which results in successfull collection of pollen and flower pollination. Green and white lateral sepals are largely fused and hidden behind the pouch. Petals are apple green and white, upper sepal is white with dark green stripes.","image":"","commonName":null,"nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":163242,"botanicalName":"<em>Paphiopedilum</em> Copper Spice gx 'Volcano'","entityDescription":"A medium-sized, clump-florming, evergreen orchid with narrowly oval, glossy, green leaves up to 25cm long and 3-4cm wide. Solitary flower, 7-10cm across, appear from the centre of the leaf rosette and are carried above foliage on 15-30cm long, upright stems. Glossy petals are rounded, dark yellow with vawy upper margin. Upper sepal is wide, usually white with pale pink and pale green and dark purple line in the centre. Both petals and sepals are covered with dark purple spotted, linear pattern.","image":"PaphiopedilumCopperSpicegxVolcano.jpg","commonName":null,"nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":217683,"botanicalName":"<em>Paphiopedilum</em> Dellaina gx","entityDescription":"A medium-sized, clump-forming orchid with narrowly-oval, evergreen leaves. Dark green leaves are mottled with pale green, approximately 15cm long and 3cm wide. One or two (rarely more) flowers are carried on 15-20cm long, upright stems emerging from the centre of the leaf rosettes. Flowering stems are covered in tiny short hairs. White, cream or pink flowers are also often pubescens. Shape and colour of flowers depends on cultivar.","image":"PaphiopedilumDellaina.jpg","commonName":nu